{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01ProYdQPZysm3538gAEgdMi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. I wrote **Q7: How efficiently generate and store embeddings for products and queries?** — `ai-engineering/answers/02-007-how-efficiently-generate-and-store-embeddings-for-products-a.md`.\n\nKey content:\n\n- **Two-path architecture**: offline batch pipeline (throughput-optimized) vs. online query embedding (latency-optimized — target < 20 ms, Redis cache for frequent queries)\n- **Batch mechanics**: 2048 inputs/call, async HTTP, ~$20 total cost for 5M products at 200 tokens each\n- **Storage**: Pinecone/Qdrant for vectors keyed on `product_id`; filterable metadata (category, price, in_stock) in a PostgreSQL sidecar — not bloating the vector payload\n- **Incremental updates**: Debezium CDC → Kafka → re-embed-and-upsert worker, 2-min freshness SLA without full re-index\n- **Critical rule**: same model at index time and query time — model mismatch breaks retrieval entirely\n- **Cost levers**: MRL (truncate to 256-dim, 6× cheaper), self-hosting on A10G (~20K embeddings/s, break-even at 500M tokens/month)\n- **4 pitfalls**: model mismatch on upgrade, single-item loop instead of batching, bloated vector payloads, no incremental update plan\n\nNext up: **Q8 — How handle hallucination when no information is found in context?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":334,"cache_read_input_tokens":58880,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":334,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f772c93-ca73-44c3-ab2a-1ca39d670427","uuid":"d9040d73-c0fb-4fa8-8d46-72e26d2f5c4c"}
